          "conf": 0.707,
          "text": "Example 1 Expand $\\left(x^2 + \\frac{3}{x}\\right)^4$, $x \\neq 0$\n\nSolution By using binomial theorem, we have\n\n$$x^2 + \\frac{3}{x} = ^4\\text{C}_0(x^2)^4 + ^4\\text{C}_1(x^2)^3 \\left(\\frac{3}{x}\\right) + ^4\\text{C}_2(x^2)^2 \\left(\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^2 + ^4\\text{C}_3(x^2) \\left(\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^3 + ^4\\text{C}_4 \\left(\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^4$$\n\n$$= x^8 + 4 \\cdot x^6 \\cdot \\frac{3}{x} + 6 \\cdot x^4 \\cdot \\frac{9}{x^2} + 4 \\cdot x^2 \\cdot \\frac{27}{x^3} + \\frac{81}{x^4}$$\n\n$$= x^8 + 12x^5 + 54x^2 + \\frac{108}{x} + \\frac{81}{x^4}$$"
        },
        {
          "order": 7,
          "label": "Solved-example",
          "type": "Text",
          "bbox_xyxy": [
            112.7,
