          ],
          "conf": 0.917,
          "text": "Solution For two numbers $a$ and $b$ if we can find numbers $q$ and $r$ such that\n$a = bq + r$, then we say that $b$ divides $a$ with $q$ as quotient and $r$ as remainder. Thus, in\norder to show that $6^n - 5n$ leaves remainder 1 when divided by 25, we prove that\n$6^n - 5n = 25k + 1$, where $k$ is some natural number."
        },
