            1177.0,
            1433.0
          ],
          "conf": 0.783,
          "text": "1. If $a$ and $b$ are distinct integers, prove that $a - b$ is a factor of $a^n - b^n$, whenever\n$n$ is a positive integer.\n[Hint write $a^n = (a - b + b)^n$ and expand]\n\n2. Evaluate $\\left(\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}\\right)^6 - \\left(\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}\\right)^6$.\n\n3. Find the value of $\\left(a^2 + \\sqrt{a^2 - 1}\\right)^4 + \\left(a^2 - \\sqrt{a^2 - 1}\\right)^4$.\n\n4. Find an approximation of $(0.99)^5$ using the first three terms of its expansion.\n\n5. Expand using Binomial Theorem $\\left(1 + \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{2}{x}\\right)^4, x \\neq 0$.\n\n6. Find the expansion of $(3x^2 - 2ax + 3a^2)^3$ using binomial theorem."
        },
        {
          "order": 5,
          "label": "Infobox",
          "type": "Text",
          "bbox_xyxy": [
            121.7,
            1447.6,
            1178.7,
            1725.6
          ],
          "conf": 0.9,
          "text": "Summary\n\nThe expansion of a binomial for any positive integral $n$ is given by Binomial\nTheorem, which is $(a + b)^n = {}^n\\text{C}_0a^n + {}^n\\text{C}_1a^{n-1}b + {}^n\\text{C}_2a^{n-2}b^2 + ... +$\n${}^n\\text{C}_{n-1}a.b^{n-1} + {}^n\\text{C}_nb^n$.\nThe coefficients of the expansions are arranged in an array. This array is\ncalled $Pascal's$ $triangle$."
        }
      ],
      "page": 7
    },
    {
